  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $f(x)=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-|x|}{2-|x|}}$\r\n$f(x)$ is defined for all $x$ satisfying $\\frac{1-|x|}{2-|x|} \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow \\frac{|x|-1}{|x|-2} \\geq 0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad|x| \\leq$ lor $|x|>2$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x \\in[-1,1]$ or $x \\in(-\\infty,-2) \\cup(2, \\infty)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x \\in(-\\infty,-2) \\cup[-1,1] \\cup(2, \\infty)$",
